### 1. Create an artist
POST http://localhost:8080/api/artists
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Weatherbys",
  "bio": "A fictional folk-rock duo, test data for the tabs app."
}

### 2. Get all artists
GET http://localhost:8080/api/artists

### 3. Create a song (replace artist.id below after running #1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/songs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "artist": { "id": 1 },
  "title": "Roads We Used to Know",
  "originalKey": "G",
  "capo": 0,
  "tempo": 96,
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "body": "[G]Somewhere over the [D]rainbow\n[Em]Way up [C]high\n[G]There's a land that I [D]heard of\n[C]Once in a [G]lullaby"
}

### 4. Get the song by id
GET http://localhost:8080/api/songs/1

### 5. Transpose it up 2 semitones (sharps)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/songs/1/transpose?semitones=2

### 6. Transpose it down 3 semitones, using flats
GET http://localhost:8080/api/songs/1/transpose?semitones=-3&useFlats=true

### 7. Search songs by title
GET http://localhost:8080/api/songs?title=roads

### 8. Search songs by artist name
GET http://localhost:8080/api/songs?artist=weather